From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sproutboat <noreply@sproutboat.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:00:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] codegen: block function declarations reach a fixpoint before
 their first use (P15)

A strict block moves each function declaration to just before the first earlier statement that mentions
it, in one pass over the block. A function moved up this way can itself mention a function declared later
that the pass had already left alone, so the callee ends up behind its caller. When the caller is
generated at its declaration (it assigns itself, the bundler's `function init_X() { return (init_X = ...)() }`
form) its nested closures are compiled before the callee is declared: the call cannot resolve the callee,
reads an env slot nobody fills, and the callee is never marked referenced, so it is dropped from the
output. At run time the call throws a TypeError with no message ("proxy is not a function" with
`--d`), or aborts with "bad function index".

Alchemy v2's Worker bundle has this shape (`init_Resource` calls `init_Output`, whose class
constructors call `proxy`, declared in between): every request of a compiled Alchemy Worker answered 500.

The pass now repeats, each function moving at most once, so mutual references stop instead of
swapping forever.

Class: upstream
Pass: generateBlock function order (P15)
Upstream: not filed
---
 compiler/codegen.js | 23 ++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/codegen.js b/compiler/codegen.js
index b331d8e061a184cfaf1752ee034266c37cabe6ff..051b364d93f2ae246db3922e78f736e25aaf0d6c 100644
--- a/compiler/codegen.js
+++ b/compiler/codegen.js
@@ -6490,13 +6490,22 @@ const generateBlock = (scope, decl) => {
   // strict block functions exist on entry: move one used earlier to just before that use (not the top, closures snapshot loop bindings)
   if (scope.strict && decl.body.some(x => x.type === 'FunctionDeclaration')) {
     const names = decl.body.map(x => identifierNames(x, new Set()));
-    for (let j = 0; j < decl.body.length; j++) {
-      const fn = decl.body[j];
-      if (fn.type !== 'FunctionDeclaration') continue;
-      const i = names.findIndex((x, k) => k < j && x.has(fn.id.name));
-      if (i === -1) continue;
-      decl.body.splice(i, 0, decl.body.splice(j, 1)[0]);
-      names.splice(i, 0, names.splice(j, 1)[0]);
+    // sproutboat: a function moved up can mention a later function that an earlier pass already left alone (a callee behind its
+    // caller is not declared yet when the caller's nested closures are generated: the call becomes an unfilled env slot). Repeat,
+    // each function moving at most once, so mutual references end instead of swapping forever.
+    const movedFns = new Set();
+    for (let again = true, pass = 0; again && pass < decl.body.length; pass++) {
+      again = false;
+      for (let j = 0; j < decl.body.length; j++) {
+        const fn = decl.body[j];
+        if (fn.type !== 'FunctionDeclaration' || movedFns.has(fn)) continue;
+        const i = names.findIndex((x, k) => k < j && x.has(fn.id.name));
+        if (i === -1) continue;
+        decl.body.splice(i, 0, decl.body.splice(j, 1)[0]);
+        names.splice(i, 0, names.splice(j, 1)[0]);
+        movedFns.add(fn);
+        again = true;
+      }
     }
   }
   for (const x of decl.body) {
